# Tag navigation

Create two members of tag a and one member of b. Use alphabetical ordering so
navigation and wraparound have predictable destinations.

    :b jj cat (available)
    :t rename-session -t 0 runner (success)
    :t new-session -d -s alpha cat (success)
    :t new-session -d -s beta cat (success)
    :t new-session -d -s gamma cat (success)
    :$ -q smth --no-base --tag a alpha (exit: 0)
    :$ -q smth --no-base --tag b beta (exit: 0)
    :$ -q smth --no-base --tag a gamma (exit: 0)
    :$ -q smth --no-base --flag alpha (exit: 0)
    :$ -q smth --no-base --flag beta (exit: 0)
    :t new-session -d -s ui 'smth --order +name' (success)
    :t resize-window -t ui:0 -x 80 -y 12 (success)
    :p ui:0.0
    :settle -d 2s (settled)

Hide the preview. C-j enters next-key mode without changing the selection;
then a skips beta and selects gamma. The tag key does not edit the query.

    :k C-p C-j
    :snap

```terminal
session:                                                                       ┃
  5/5 | [C-s] ↓n | [C-r] repo: none                                            ┃
▌■ alpha                                 a                                     ┃
 ■ beta                                  b                                     ┃
 ■ gamma                                 a                                     ┃
 ■ runner                                                                      ┃
 ■ ui                                                                          ┃
                                                                               ┃
                                                                               ┃
                                                                               ┃
                                                                               ┃
                                                          next tag [C-g] cancel┃
```

    :k a
    :snap

```terminal
session:                                                                       ┃
  5/5 | [C-s] ↓n | [C-r] repo: none                                            ┃
 ■ alpha                                 a                                     ┃
 ■ beta                                  b                                     ┃
▌■ gamma                                 a                                     ┃
 ■ runner                                                                      ┃
 ■ ui                                                                          ┃
                                                                               ┃
                                                                               ┃
                                                                               ┃
                                                                               ┃
 [C-x] close, [C-f] flag, [C-t] tags: a                                        ┃
```

Next wraps to alpha, and previous wraps back to gamma. A tag with no members
leaves gamma selected. An invalid key cancels without editing the query.

    :k C-j a
    :snap

```terminal
session:                                                                       ┃
  5/5 | [C-s] ↓n | [C-r] repo: none                                            ┃
▌■ alpha                                 a                                     ┃
